                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_285">Kirkham, Yorkshire.
                        Augustinian priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church</orgName><p><q>Liber
                           s(an)c(t) T(ri)nitatis de Kirkeha(m) / In hoc volumi(n)e (con)tinent(ur)
                           vii libri. / Joh(anne)s heremita de .x. coll(ati)o(n)ib(us) / ... </q>,
                        above list of contents on flyleaf.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">? John Nettleton (d. 1597) of Hutton
                     Cranswick, collector of manuscripts from Yorkshire monasteries; inscribed 'dono
                     nettelton'.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir John Savile (1545–1607), brother of Sir
                     Henry Savile; sold at Sotheby's, 6 February 1861, lot 42.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir Thomas Phillipps (1792–1872); his 25421,
                     sold at Sotheby's, 17 May 1897, lot 38 to Ellis (£24.10.0). This was the last
                     known provenance according to the first edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1941), p. 59.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir John Arthur Brooke; sold at Sotheby's, 25
                     May 1921, lot 840, bought by Davis and Orioli. This was the last known
                     provenance according to the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1964), p. 106.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Laurence W. Hodson, with his
                     book-label.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'The property of a Gentleman', sold at
                     Sotheby's, 8 December 1981, lot 89 (with plate). Compare also Schoenberg
                     Database of Manuscripts <ref
                        target="https://sdbm.library.upenn.edu/manuscripts/844"
                     >SDBM_MS_844</ref></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Now Los Angeles, Dr P. F. Slawson' according
                     the supplement to Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1987), p. 41. In MLGB3
                     (2009-2015), the book reverted to being untraced.</provenance>
               </history>
